.TH "libnvmf_exclusion_list_for_each" 9 "libnvmf_exclusion_list_for_each" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_exclusion_list_for_each \- iterate over exclusion list names.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_exclusion_list_for_each
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "void (*callback)(const char *name, void *user_data) "  ","
.BI "void *user_data "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
libnvme global context; must not be NULL
.IP "callback" 12
called for each .conf file; name is basename without .conf suffix
.IP "user_data" 12
caller context passed to \fIcallback\fP
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, negative errno on error.
Returns 0 when the directory does not exist (nothing excluded).
